# === What this species carries (theory, NOT operations) ===
#
# Per Mara math §2.1 + Reed spec §6.2 the substrate has drafted
# the theory carriers with full mathematical grounding. This
# species-decl lands them as first-class substrate-decl. The
# carrier bodies + composition axioms + decidability discharge
# discharge in the follow-up canonical spec (deferred by design
# per Alex 2026-07-17 arbitration).
#
# Predicate carriers (per math §2.1):
#   - liquid_qualifier — a predicate + arity carrier at the
#      qualifier-fragment altitude. Each qualifier is one
#      predicate the substrate can decide against a value_var
#      + base_type binding.
#   - qualifier_set — a finite set Q of liquid_qualifiers at a
#      given altitude. Q_mirror per math §2.2 = landed
#      `@epistemologic/property/*` + `@epistemologic/pact/*`
#      predicates (~40 as of 2026-07-05).
#   - refinement_predicate — a conjunction of qualifiers over a
#      value_var + base_type. The substrate-decl'd form of the
#      refinement-type refinement.
#   - liquid_claim — an alias for doc_claim viewed through the
#      refinement-type lens; the input to the extraction
#      operational subspecies.
#   - liquid_verdict — the four/five-valued verdict at doc/liquid
#      altitude (per math §2.1 + extraction subspecies §2). At
#      extraction subspecies discharges to `satisfiable |
#      unsatisfiable | partial | unextractable`; at theory
#      altitude carries additionally a decidable-fragment marker.
#
# Composition axioms (per math §2 + Reed spec §5):
#   - conjunction (∧): refinement_predicate ∧ refinement_predicate
#      → refinement_predicate (finite qualifier_set union).
#   - implication (⇒): refinement_predicate ⇒ refinement_predicate
#      via spectral Laplacian eigenvalue check (NOT SMT). The
#      substrate-honest replacement for the SMT decision procedure
#      the SOTA (LiquidHaskell, Flux, F*) uses.
#   - universal (∀): quantification over refinement predicates in
#      a qualifier_set. Discharge via property-Laplacian per
#      Reed spec §5.
#
# Decidability boundary (per math §6.1 theorem + Seam correction):
#   - Sub-Turing per recognition #107 — the substrate GUARANTEES
#      what Alive2 and CompCert PROVE case-by-case. The
#      refinement-predicate fragment is decidable at the shard-
#      decl altitude; extraction from arbitrary text is @io-
#      boundary Turing-complete (Seam `20d0c13` §5 C2 correction
#      landed at math §6.1).
#   - Rice-safe by construction on byte-visible content: the
#      bilateral degenerate case (byte-check sentinel) is Rice-
#      safe by construction; more general refinement composition
#      inherits Rice-safety when qualifier bodies are byte-visible
#      predicates on content-addressed refs. Composition-preserves-
#      Rice-safety is a follow-up conjecture the deferred-by-design
#      canonical spec discharges.
#
# === Connection to @epistemologic/pact/bilateral ===
#
# Per recognition candidate #R-bilateral-is-degenerate-liquid-with-
# byte-check-predicate (surfaced this tick; holds at candidate
# strength): every landed `bilateral <name> { sentinel "..."
# arity N }` block (~30 landed arms across 8 shard groups per
# `shards/epistemologic/pact/bilateral.mirror:44-88`) IS a single-
# qualifier refinement_predicate where the qualifier is
# `oid_contains(sentinel)`. The bilateral discipline is @liquid's
# byte-check subspecies at the pact altitude.
#
# The 2026-07-17 paradigmatic reframe at `shards/epistemologic/
# pact/bilateral.mirror:451-707` (Alex 2026-07-17 Path A ratified)
# generalized the byte-check bilateral to `@bilateral(A, B)` as
# `@glue`-`@metalogue` composition. That reframe extends the
# degenerate-liquid discipline to arbitrary correspondence
# translation; the theory this species declares grounds the
# refinement-predicate shape both readings share.
#
# === Connection to the extraction subspecies ===
#
# `@epistemologic/liquid/extraction` (migrated this tick from the
# older `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` per Alex 2026-07-17
# Q-C arbitration; see `shards/epistemologic/liquid/extraction.
# mirror`) is the OPERATIONAL subspecies UNDER this theory. The
# extraction operation lowers `doc_claim` to a splinter(ast)
# fragment carrying a refinement_predicate this theory defines.
# Extraction is a subspecies of theory, NOT a peer; recognition
# candidate #R-extraction-is-liquid-subspecies-not-liquid-peer
# holds at candidate strength.
#
# === Path-namespace property ===
#
# This file at `shards/epistemologic/liquid.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/liquid` at species-depth 1 under @epistemologic
# per @epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace. Sibling species
# at the same depth: @epistemologic/reality, @epistemologic/pact,
# @epistemologic/property, @epistemologic/cybernetic,
# @epistemologic/math, @epistemologic/neutrosophic,
# @epistemologic/spectral_triple.
#
# === Recognition candidates surfaced (NOT ratified) ===
#
# All hold at candidate strength; await Alex adjudication at a
# future tick. Named here per Mara discipline surface for later
# review:
#
#   - #R-epistemologic-liquid-is-theory-carrier-sibling-to-
#      reality-pact-property-cybernetic — this species-decl's
#      altitude claim.
#   - #R-extraction-is-liquid-subspecies-not-liquid-peer —
